---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBasePath } from '../lib/site-paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn how Terapixel Games publishes original browser games, labels release status, and keeps player support clear."
>
  <div class="shell stack">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="page-title">About Terapixel Games</h1>
      <p class="page-copy">
        Terapixel Games is a small browser-game publisher focused on original arcade, puzzle, and card games that run in
        modern web browsers. The site exists for players who want working games, clear instructions, honest release status,
        and a direct way to contact the studio when something needs attention.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content-grid" aria-label="Studio principles">
      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>What We Make</h2>
        <p>
          We publish lightweight web games with immediate controls, readable goals, and short repeatable runs. The current
          live library includes arcade movement, color-matching puzzle, and speed-focused card games exported for desktop
          and mobile browsers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>How We Label Releases</h2>
        <p>
          Public game pages have active launch links, fullscreen paths, and written instructions. Unreleased projects stay
          out of public navigation and the sitemap until they provide enough value for players.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>What Players Can Expect</h2>
        <p>
          Every live game page should explain the core loop, controls, practical play tips, and what kind of player the
          game is for before asking anyone to launch fullscreen. If something breaks, the Support and Contact pages provide
          a direct email channel.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>Editorial Standard</h2>
        <p>
          We keep site copy specific to games we operate, avoid fake download claims, and separate publisher information
          from ads, account tools, and shop experiments. The goal is a site that is useful with or without monetization.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="glass-panel text-panel">
        <h2>Review and Maintenance</h2>
        <p>
          We review public pages for broken links, misleading labels, thin copy, and unclear calls to action before asking
          advertising partners to evaluate the site. Pages that are not ready for public discovery are kept out of the
          sitemap until they provide enough value for visitors.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="glass-panel text-panel" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact the Studio</h2>
      <p>
        For gameplay reports, privacy questions, or partnership inquiries, email
        <a href="mailto:support@terapixel.games">support@terapixel.games</a> or use the
        <a href={withBasePath('/support')}>Support page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
